# Server data

The access token is a module variable in `lib/auth/access-token.ts`. It is never written to `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, or a JavaScript-readable cookie.

`lib/api/http-client.ts` sends `credentials: "include"`, sets `Authorization` when a token exists, and on `401` calls `POST /auth/refresh` once and retries the original request once. A failed refresh clears the token and sends the admin to `/login`.

Read `success`, `message`, `data`, and `meta`. Do not invent a second envelope.

| Key | Data | Stale time |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `["auth", "me"]` | current admin | 30s default |
| `["doctors", query]` | doctor page | 30s |
| `["doctors", "facets"]` | filter values | 30s |
| `["doctors", id]` | doctor detail | 30s |
| `["patients", query]` | patient page, including `doctorId` | 30s |
| `["dashboard", from, to]` | every tile and chart | 60s |

After a doctor write, invalidate `["doctors"]`. After a patient write or delete, invalidate `["patients"]`, `["doctors", doctorId]`, and `["dashboard"]`.

Login, logout, refresh, mutations, filter text, page, dialogs, and the date range are not queries. Debounce search text before it enters a query key. Edit a patient from the row already loaded. Do not add `GET /patients/:id` to open the dialog.

Chart labels print the API's `YYYY-MM-DD` string. Do not pass that string through `new Date()`.
